250ceeba8931f3f4600348602fd19376eedcf6ca6d48da04aacc06","event_uuid":"0c978082-d67c-40a8-b6a3-f9406d3d18dd","position":{"commit_sha":"b807bd673456372cb413ad6484b4a73c1c0e6127","position":"1794936843861810560-0c978082-d67c-40a8-b6a3-f9406d3d18dd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"db5bc8ec2b599009aff6584addceba2bee09dc0feef682d1e38a7c55a097e08e","event_uuid":"50c83dbe-9e2d-4558-806e-cec3d0c86c37","position":{"commit_sha":"73d530ea9062a5cc6f468d29cfb068fde3a6604c","position":"1794936894414723880-50c83dbe-9e2d-4558-806e-cec3d0c86c37"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"db217e58b73111caee3f1119b8bc7730f58d580b7a13bf4dd57e16472c41fe93","event_uuid":"42e9f437-1562-4f2a-b84c-9cf08e3cb6e5","position":{"commit_sha":"73d530ea9062a5cc6f468d29cfb068fde3a6604c","position":"1794936894434250711-42e9f437-1562-4f2a-b84c-9cf08e3cb6e5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"2a462b92767c6c3dc9c577406eb0908a89aa4d79b765315c142db5ee0246b998","event_uuid":"30180167-4cdc-41bb-998d-36d7fa606d64","position":{"commit_sha":"c4f07d5be3395fb891fda628daeedbcef0542f80","position":"1794936963377619175-30180167-4cdc-41bb-998d-36d7fa606d64"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review certified (57d45053272). Process note: I wrote the two regression tests and the fix in worktree fix-reclaim-anchor while the plan review was running, before claiming; the ticket was claimed after certification and before commit 6f620bc4a0d. Both new tests failed before the fix (anchor not an ancestor of HEAD; the unsigned replayed event was grandfathered and verify-identity exited 0) and pass after it; all 15 collapse tests pass. lint, typecheck and C901 clean. make verify running before the Gerrit push.","timestamp":1794936963377619175}],"created_at":1794936353365015891,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a2420540-4b7a-43bc-8970-6974502c6a8e","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8dc4-1541-92a7-4351"}],"description":"## Symptom\n\nWhen a collapse replays any commit above the boundary, the ledger-anchor commit is not an ancestor of the rewritten tip. The rewritten branch runs checkpoint → first replayed commit. The ledger anchor is a side child of the checkpoint that nothing references, and the collapse deletes its scratch ref, so the anchor ends up unreachable.\n\n`CollapseResult.enforce_since` is that anchor. `verify_authorship._is_enforced` (`src/rebar/_commands/verify_authorship.py:258`) enforces an event only when `git merge-base --is-ancestor <since_ref> <event commit>` succeeds. That never happens for an unreachable anchor, so every event in the rewritten history is grandfathered. `verify-identity` then passes without checking any signature.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Synthetic probe, 2026-11-17.** Built from `tests/unit/test_reclaim_collapse.py::_build_collapsible_store`, with 1 replayed commit. The result was `anchor_is_ancestor_of_tip False` and `enforce_since == ledger_anchor_sha True`. The same result came from the current engine (origin/main 57d45053272) and from the original S1 engine (a758402f065, ticket `filmable-crushing-nighthawk`). The defect predates the streamed rewrite (`silk-unpleasant-jackal`), which reproduced the original behaviour exactly.\n- **Real-scale dry run, 2026-11-16.** On a TMPDIR copy of `origin/tickets` at e7a0476397f, the rewritten root 9ecfe8768a5 has exactly one child, b04372602ca. That child is a replayed `reconciler: persist binding-store snapshot` commit. `git log --grep \"reconcile authorship ledger\" tickets` finds nothing.\n- **Why the existing test passes.** `test_enforce_since_reanchor_makes_verify_authorship_clean` collapses with the tip equal to the boundary. No commit is replayed, so the anchor is the tip and the defect is hidden.\n\n## Cause\n\nIn `_StreamedRewrite._replay` (`src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_collapse.py:507`), a replayed commit's parents go through `self.old_to_new`, and `_write_base` maps the boundary to the checkpoint (`self._map(boundary, self.checkpoint_sha)`). A replayed commit whose original parent is the boundary is therefore parented on the checkpoint, not on the ledger anchor (`self.current_tip` at that point).\n\n## Approach\n\nIn `_replay`, map a parent equal to the boundary to `self.ledger_anchor_sha` instead of `old_to_new[boundary]`. Leave `old_to_new[boundary] = checkpoint_sha` unchanged. The SNAPSHOT ledger rewrites (`_map_old_commit`) still resolve below-boundary events to the checkpoint, which stays an ancestor of every rewritten commit through the anchor.\n\nThe anchor's tree is the boundary tree plus the re-resolved SNAPSHOTs. Its `source_of` is already the boundary, and its `k_of` is 0. A child of the anchor therefore diffs against the boundary and inherits the anchor's rewritten SNAPSHOT bytes. It re-resolves only the SNAPSHOTs that reference commits mapped after the anchor, which is the same dirty rule the engine already applies.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_collapse.py`: the parent mapping in `_StreamedRewrite._replay`.\n- `tests/unit/test_reclaim_collapse.py`: the regression tests below.\n\n## Testing\n\nTDD, red first, on throwaway shadow repositories under `tmp_path`.\n\n- Ancestry: after `_build_collapsible_store` plus an applied collapse (1 replayed commit), `git merge-base --is-ancestor <ledger_anchor_sha> HEAD` succeeds and the anchor is the first parent of the first replayed commit.\n- Enforcement: an unsigned replayed event fails `python -m rebar verify-identity --all` under `REBAR_IDENTITY_REQUIRE_AUTHENTICATED=1` and `REBAR_IDENTITY_ENFORCE_SINCE=<enforce_since>` (exit non-zero, the event counted unsigned). Below-boundary events stay grandfathered. This is the failure path the existing test cannot see.\n- `test_streamed_engine_matches_the_rewrite_oracle` keeps passing. Its expectations are parent counts and SNAPSHOT SHA mappings, and both still hold.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] After a collapse that replays at least one commit, `ledger_anchor_sha` is an ancestor of `rewritten_tip`, and `enforce_since` names a commit on the rewritten branch. The new ancestry test shows this.\n- [ ] With replayed commits and `REBAR_IDENTITY_ENFORCE_SINCE=<enforce_since>`, `verify-identity --all` enforces the replayed events. The new enforcement test shows an unsigned replayed event failing the gate.\n- [ ] Every test in `tests/unit/test_reclaim_collapse.py` passes.\n- [ ] `make verify` is run and any failure is fixed or shown environmental; the Gerrit change gets `Verified +1`; `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` exit 0.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_collapse.py","reason":"Parent a replayed commit whose original parent is the boundary on the ledger anchor."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_reclaim_collapse.py","reason":"Ancestry and enforcement regression tests for replayed commits."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","536b-8930-b922-4063"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"536b-8930-b922-4063","parent_status_uuid":"50c83dbe-9e2d-4558-806e-cec3d0c86c37","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"a67d-5760-9dd4-4bd2","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reclaim collapse leaves the ledger-anchor commit off the rewritten branch, so enforce_since grandfathers every event","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["37b7701c-78f2-4af6-90c8-186114aeff7d","a2420540-4b7a-43bc-8970-6974502c6a8e","47a0f6f3-1e7e-404b-aea0-5baca2695ab0","298aedec-3923-45a2-9b73-066a55e33a4e","0c978082-d67c-40a8-b6a3-f9406d3d18dd","50c83dbe-9e2d-4558-806e-cec3d0c86c37","42e9f437-1562-4f2a-b84c-9cf08e3cb6e5","30180167-4cdc-41bb-998d-36d7fa606d64"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794936963377619176,"uuid":"99532e97-50d1-4566-b6b1-e77fa95e1075"}